{"type":"npc","name":"Cathartic Slime","folder":null,"system":{"attributes":{"hp":{"value":150,"temp":0,"max":150,"details":""},"ac":{"value":12,"details":""},"allSaves":{"value":""},"speed":{"value":20,"otherSpeeds":[{"type":"swim","value":20}],"details":""},"immunities":[{"type":"critical-hits","exceptions":[]},{"type":"precision","exceptions":[]},{"type":"unconscious","exceptions":[]},{"type":"visual","exceptions":[]}],"weaknesses":[{"type":"fire","value":5,"exceptions":[]}]},"initiative":{"statistic":"perception"},"details":{"languages":{"value":[],"details":"Common cant speak any language"},"level":{"value":5},"blurb":"","publicNotes":"<p>Cathartic slimes live near the edges of bodies of water, particularly ones where intelligent creatures swim. When such a creature enters the water, the slime approaches to feed on its emotions. Though the feelings the creature is currently experiencing can provide slight nourishment, the slimes prefer to flood their prey's minds with memories that provoke strong emotions. Some cathartic slimes focus on a particular emotion, while others have a varied diet.</p><p>Occasionally, a cathartic slime gets into primary water sources like wells and public water supplies and is accidentally ingested by entire communities. This can cause significant troubles as the community is overcome with grief, fear, or euphoria.</p><p>If a cathartic slime spends long enough feeding on the same creature, the emotions associated with their memories are forever dulled. Some people deliberately seek out cathartic slimes with particular emotional preferences, either to relive the joy of their best memories or to endure temporary pain to reduce the sting of their worst ones.</p><h2>Last Meal</h2><p>Cathartic slime eats emotions, not creatures, and has no use for the dead. It doesn't go out of its way to kill creatures, preferring to reuse a creature's mind for as long as strong feelings can be wrung out of it. However, a cathartic slime's own emotions—especially fear, anger, and self-preservation—are perfectly well-developed. If hurt or angered, a slime will try to destroy the creature that threatens it. As a side benefit, a creature about to be drowned or crushed by a cathartic slime usually experiences many delicious emotions, such as fear, horror, and disgust, before their terrible end.</p><h2>Suggested Monster Parts</h2><p><strong>Monster Parts</strong> 18/45/80 gp</p><p><strong>Eligible Refinements</strong> weapons (bludgeoning), perception item, skill items (Athletics, Stealth)</p><p><strong>Eligible Imbued Properties</strong> body, bane, constitution, energy resistant (fire, vitality), fortification, mind, mind shield, strength, throwing, water, wild</p>","privateNotes":"","publication":{"title":"Battlezoo Bestiary: Elemental Storm (Pathfinder)","authors":"Sam Coleman","license":"ORC","remaster":true}},"resources":{},"_migration":{"version":0.942,"previous":{"schema":0.941,"foundry":"13.347","system":"7.3.1"}},"abilities":{"str":{"mod":4},"dex":{"mod":1},"con":{"mod":5},"int":{"mod":0},"wis":{"mod":2},"cha":{"mod":2}},"perception":{"details":"","mod":9,"senses":[{"type":"thoughtsense","acuity":"imprecise","range":120}],"vision":false},"saves":{"fortitude":{"value":14,"saveDetail":""},"reflex":{"value":10,"saveDetail":""},"will":{"value":11,"saveDetail":""}},"skills":{"athletics":{"base":11},"stealth":{"base":10}},"traits":{"value":["amphibious","ooze","water"],"rarity":"uncommon","size":{"value":"med"}}},"_id":"ApOANbPfkpqEnY1A","img":"modules/battlezoo-bestiary-es-pf2e/assets/portraits/cathartic-slime.webp","prototypeToken":{"name":"Cathartic Slime","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false,"width":1,"height":1,"texture":{"src":"modules/battlezoo-bestiary-es-pf2e/assets/tokens/cathartic-slime.webp","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"offsetX":0,"offsetY":0,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"rotation":0,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":